{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The mounting tape feels like a natural next choice because it offers another way to attach things where my magnetic hooks cannot hold.",
    "The caster wheels relate to moving heavy things, like my hand truck, but I would only choose them if I needed wheels and knew the mounts would fit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The measuring tools, pressure gauge and thermometer require specific tasks I have not shown a need for; buying screws and hooks does not give me a reason to use them.",
    "The filament, cleaner, sanding blocks and mesh serve projects I am not currently pursuing, so their general usefulness is not enough to make me choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in fastening and mounting seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop supply.",
    "My older hand truck purchase seems to suggest more ongoing equipment needs than I actually have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent hooks, washers and screws point toward attaching and securing things, which makes another practical mounting option more relevant than specialized instruments.",
    "I rarely buy without a clear use, and related equipment still needs to fit what I own before I would choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions partly recognized my practical hardware needs but broadened my recent fastening and mounting interest into unrelated workshop tasks."
}"}
